WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.801
-I haven't seen you,
because last time I saw you,

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.167
we were Zooming on our show.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:05.701
-That's right.
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.934
-And you were about to film
"Halston" in New York City.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.400
-Oh, yeah.
-And everything got shut down.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.200
-How is it to be back,
with the audience and such?

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.701
-It's the greatest thing.
Doesn't it feel great?

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.000
It's totally night and day.
-The Roots, the band.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.167
-The Roots. Everyone's here.
It's night and day.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:19.901
-Fantastic.
-I want to say congrats,

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.300
'cause you ended up
resuming filming.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.734
-Can I say congrats to Questlove
for his documentary?

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.434
-Oh, yeah.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.601
-Beautiful.

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:30.667
-I mean, of course,
congratulations to Questlove.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:33.167
But congratulations to you.
You won an Emmy for "Halston."

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.067
-Oh, yeah.
-Come on.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:37.834
Come on.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:40.067
-It's nice. But he made
a really beautiful film.

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:42.100
-He did, yeah.
-That was pretty impressive.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.801
-You know, every time you're
on the show, I eventually start

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.567
to talk to you
about motorcycles,

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:47.901
'cause I'm interested in them,

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:50.601
and you did a very dangerous
stunt for us one time.

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:53.267
-That's right!
-Yeah. Remember that one?

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:55.100
-I loved -- I had forgotten
all about that. That's right.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.501
-We should put that on --
back on YouTube,

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:57.968
'cause that was
really dangerous.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:01.701
-I jumped over --
I attempted a very dangerous --

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:03.634
You were talking about --
-Don't try this at home.

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:04.934
-You were talking
about Tom Cruise earlier.

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:06.334
-Yeah. Doing his own stunts.

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.400
-Well, I've never seen Tom
Cruise do something like this.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.801
-Yeah.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:13.334
-I jumped over
an Obi-Wan Kenobi doll.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.567
-Yeah.

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.367
A tiny figurine,
like, about that size.

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:18.834
-Yeah. On a -- on a motorcycle.
-On a motorcycle.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.200
-It was about that size.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.267
And I'm not sure if you
jumped over it or through it.

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.100
But either way, you kind of...

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.767
The wheel had maybe
this much clearance.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:26.834
-Yeah.
-It was amazing.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:27.968
And we put it in slow motion.

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.234
-I got all those different
angles and stuff.

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:31.634
-You did. You put a lot
of work into that.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.334
-Anouk did it with me,
my little kid.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:37.067
We had like, different --
We had an iPad and two phones.

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.868
And we edited it in slow motion.
-I loved it.

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:40.934
-Oh, it was great.
-We'll tweet about it

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.901
'cause it was actually worth it.
It was so good.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.767
But I -- I never wanted --
I never --

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.667
Well, I never have asked you,
what got you into motorcycles?

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:50.167
Was it, like -- Do you remember
your first motorcycle?

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.734
-I remember the first time
I rode one, but I think

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:55.567
I was already -- I used to watch
old Elvis Presley movies.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:56.701
-Yeah.

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:59.133
-My favorite film,
even as a little kid,

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.767
was "The Great Escape,"
and Steve McQueen --

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.267
I had one of those wind-up
Evel Knievel toys.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.868
-Yes.
-You remember that?

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:07.167
-Sure, and you pull
the rip thing, and it'd go --

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:09.067
-And off it goes.
So -- I don't know.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.267
The motorcycle was, like,

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:13.467
already an object of desire
to me, I guess.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:16.667
-Yeah.
-And then my dad was --

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:20.300
was the chairman of this
charity organization called

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.267
the Round Table in Crieff,
where I come from.

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.200
And he -- he did this thing
where he --

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.868
local kids would write to him,
and he'd like -- you know --

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.868
Somebody wanted
to ride a motorbike,

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.000
and he would make that happen.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.367
So we went down.
I went with him.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.167
-That's nice.
-And then this little kid

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:35.667
got to ride around -- and
I was just a little kid, too --

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:37.067
on this little motorbike.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:40.267
Like, a little 50cc
twist-and-go bike.

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.033
And after he'd finished
and went home,

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:43.601
my dad said,
"Do you want a go?"

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:47.434
And I -- I just --
My life changed on that moment,

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:50.133
'cause I never got over --
I never got over it.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.634
-Really?
-I'm still the same now.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:52.834
Like I'm -- I get on my bike.

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.501
I'm like,
"Are they letting me do this?"

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:56.501
Like, "Am I allowed to do...?"
-Really, yeah.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:58.300
-It feels so much fun,
it should be illegal, really,

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.067
riding a motorbike.
-Yeah.

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:02.167
I mean, I could never
be that guy.

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:05.200
I'm more of a person that sits
in the truck and watches.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.534
-In your electric truck.
-In the -- yeah, in the fr--

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:10.334
If I park it,
I could sit in the frunk

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:12.434
and watch you ride.

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:14.300
'Cause it's just rad.
-It's cool.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.133
Me and Charlie, did --
My mate and I did a trip

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:20.133
from the bottom of South America
to L.A. on electric motorbikes.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.767
-Oh, yeah!
-Yeah, a long way up.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.033
I think we talked about it.
-We did. How was it?

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:25.267
Did you feel --
-It was good.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:26.667
It was --
The bikes are beautiful.

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:28.501
Plugging them in, in Patagonia
is an issue,

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:29.901
'cause there's nowhere
to plug them in, but...

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:31.901
-If I'm next to you
in the truck,

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.234
you could plug in and charge it!

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:35.100
-I could plug in your frunk!
-Dude, come on, bud.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.000
-Come on. Let's do another one.
-I'm there for you!

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.167
I am there for you!
[ Applause ]

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.067
Let's talk about the --

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.200
your new "Star Wars" series,
"Obi-Wan Kenobi."

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.767
I mean, I'm freaking out!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:47.701
Fans are freaking out
everywhere.

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:50.334
-Yeah.
-This is your first time back

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:52.968
as Obi-Wan Kenobi in 17 years.

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:54.467
Does that make sense?

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:57.033
-Yeah, the -- We finished
the third one in 2003.

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:58.434
-Oh, my goodness.

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:00.300
-So it's a long time ago.
But it was so fun.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.868
It was just like -- I went --

00:04:01.868 --> 00:04:04.434
The first thing I had to do
was go and do, like, a --

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:07.467
I had to read with other actors
for two roles.

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:09.000
And there was like six actors.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.000
So we borrowed
"The Mandalorian" set

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.267
and we went in on a Sunday
when they had a day off.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.901
And they had a bit of their set,
and their crew were there.

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.834
And I -- I went down,
and there was --

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.334
I went to this dressing room,

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:22.434
and there was this sort of
Obi-Wan-esque costume, you know?

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:24.400
They'd thrown --
sort of cobbled it together.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.200
-Yeah.
-And I put it on, and that was

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.634
kind of breathtaking, after 17
years, looking in the mirror.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:32.033
But then I went on and I started
reading with these other actors,

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:34.834
and I totally didn't have
his voice at all.

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:36.534
It was really bad.
I was just doing this sort of

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:39.501
vague English accent,
and it didn't sound at all

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:41.334
like Obi-Wan Kenobi.
-So, all the crew were like...

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:42.767
-Yeah.
-..."Who the heck is this guy?"

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:44.300
-They were quite excited
when I walked on.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.868
I could feel that they were
quite excited.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:48.033
But then they were
immediately disappointed.

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:49.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:51.300
-But then you went --
you went --

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.767
-And I had to do some homework.

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:54.567
I just had to go back,
and, like,

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.334
watch lots of
Alec Guinness movies

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:58.334
and watch all
the original films and...

00:04:58.334 --> 00:04:59.667
I got back into it.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.100
It was good.
It was really good fun.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.234
-You do something that I heard
that's very funny.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:06.100
You sometimes do, like,
a Jedi-type hand move,

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.267
where you pretend
to use the Force,

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.234
but just for your own amusement.

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:13.167
Do you know what I'm talking
about? Like, like --

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.734
-Yeah, I know,
like, an automatic door.

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:17.634
I can't help myself.

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:18.901
-Dude, I would freak out if I --

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.834
Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:05:20.834 --> 00:05:22.968
You go to the grocery store?
-In the airport or something.

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.334
You know, there's always like --

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:26.300
In the airport,
there's always automatic doors.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.968
I always -- I always do it
for myself, but...

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:30.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:33.567
But I also hope somebody
sees me do it, you know?

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:35.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.868
-Next time
you see Ewan McGregor,

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:38.033
see if you can see him do it.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.300
There's lots more to talk about.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.133
I want to show a clip
from "Obi-Wan Kenobi."

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:42.901
More with Ewan McGregor
when we come back.

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:44.467
Stick around, everybody.

